  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Binomial Expansions: coefficient of one term</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 1.2: Find the coefficient of x^r in (a + bx)^n, n = 6 to 9, using Pascal's triangle.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 5, Section C, Exercise C, question 6 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 2 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: new brackets, powers and terms, randomised; the row of Pascal's triangle replaces the formula.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
